      "id": "rdls_hzd-jrc_drmkc_windstorms",
      "title": "Probabilistic Windstorm Hazard Event Set for Europe",
      "description": "Windstorm hazard event set containing maximum wind gust speed per event on a 4.4 km geographical grid.",
      "risk_data_type": [
        "hazard"
      ],
      "publisher": {
        "name": "Federal Institute of Technology in Zurich (ETH Zurich)",
        "url": "http://www.wcr.ethz.ch/"
      },
      "version": "1",
      "purpose": "Assessment of probabilistic windstorm hazard across Europe with maximum wind gust speed data for risk and damage evaluation.",
      "project": {
        "name": "Risk Data Hub",
        "url": "https://drmkc.jrc.ec.europa.eu/risk-data-hub#/"
      },
      "details": "This data archive is publishing a probabilistic extension of the historic windstorm hazard event set by Windstorm Information Service. The methodology used to create this data archive is documented in the publication: \"Comparing an insurer's perspective on building damages with modelled damages from pan-European winter windstorm event sets: a case study from Zurich, Switzerland\" by Welker, Ch, Roosli, T and Bresch D N (2021).Windstorm hazard event set containing maximum wind gust speed per event on a 4.4 km geographical grid. The hazard event set covers Europe, but is divided into one file per country (ISO 3166-1 definition). Each file contains Latitude and Longitude coordinates describing the geographical grid. Event-ID and further metadata describing each event and a matrix reporting the maximum wind gust speed in Meters per Second [m/s] per event and grid coordinate.",
      "contact_point": {
